# 10. Final decision

**I approve the overall direction of your plan, subject to the revisions above.**

The most important decisions are:

- Never fabricate a muhurat or festival date.
- Never treat a formatted timing string as proof that a calculation is verified.
- Validate astronomical calculations separately from regional observance rules.
- Do not change the existing UI unnecessarily.
- Do not claim build, test, privacy, or release success without evidence.

The reference methodology should also be documented accurately. The Indian Meteorological Department provides useful primary material through its [Indian Astronomical Ephemeris]([Indian Astronomical Ephemeris](https://mausam.imd.gov.in/responsive/indianAstronomicalEphemeris.php?utm_source=chatgpt.com)) and [Rashtriya Panchang]([Rashtriya Panchang](https://mausam.imd.gov.in/responsive/rashtriyPanchang.php?utm_source=chatgpt.com)) publications.

**My recommendation is to approve the revised plan, conduct the read-only review in Google AI Studio, and then begin Pass 1.** We should not proceed directly to broad implementation until the actual project, its build workflow, and the baseline failures are established.